{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And she shall sit.</b> Like לא אכלתי באני (Deuteronomy 26:14), and it is from the second [person] feminine, and the word came like וסרו הצפרדעים (Exodus 8:7), milra." "<b>Her gates.</b> It returns to Zion, which is mentioned at the beginning of the pericope, and the meaning is the lack of males." "<b>And she shall be emptied.</b> Like נקיון שנים (Gen. 24:55) [i.e. wait a while]." "<b>She shall sit on the ground.</b> It returns to Zion."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The lemma 'ואנו' appears to correspond to 'ונקתה' or another word in the verse; preserved as in source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:20.763610809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}